            "type": "callout",
            "tone": "definition",
            "title": "Microscopic events",
            "text": "Microscopic events are the phenomena that cannot be observed with the naked eye."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The collisions between molecules, the breaking and forming of bonds, the rearrangement of atoms in molecules, and the loss or gain of electrons are examples of microscopic events."
          }
        ]
      }
    }
